Step 2 — Reproduce one failure and classify it

Pick the single most important tool/script that's being blocked, run it once, and capture exactly what happens. The symptom maps to a layer:

┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     What you see                      │  The layer that fired   │               What it means for your approach                │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ File renamed/removed the instant it's written to disk │ Statrop tools to disk; go in-memory                       │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Tool starts, then gets killed mid-run                 │ Behavioral (STAR)       │ Slow down, split activity, change the behavior, not the file │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Script dies immediately with an AMSI/"blocked" error  │ AMSI/CLR hook           │ AMSI bypass or run .NET unmanaged                            │
├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Nothing blocks locally but SOC calls you              │ Telemetry only          │ You're already "through" — now tune for quiet                │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Run your tool and immediately check the agent's own view if you have console access; if not, note the timing and the exact error.
